tall via `localstore`. Every Build entry is byte-identical for identical inputs; every Decode entry enforces the closed shape. Row-21 exclusion allowlist (`hosttrust` matchers) enforced at raw-entry and capture-item construction with per-class negatives.\\n+- OWNERSHIP: `canonicaljson` keeps its `rejectUnsupportedImmutableObjectShape` rows (that table's census pins every row); this package is the validating owner and reuses `Canonicalize` (byte transform), `CalculateObjectIdentity` plus local claim comparisons (blobs; never the attesting `VerifyObjectIdentity` entry — only the test fixture calls it — per the provhost no-attestation bound), `sessadapter.DecodeTuple`, the `environ` scalar gate set via delegating wrappers, `scalar`, `hosttrust`, and `localstore.PutBlob`. No `internal/traceability` edit (FINAL leaf carries bindings + re-pin); clause map in `internal/clonebundle/TRACEABILITY.md`.\\n+- EVIDENCE: package suite green (87.1% statements), 66 narrowing mutants KILLED + harmless control SURVIVED (`testdata/mutant_harness.py --log-dir`, one raw log per plant with subprocess exit, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`); `TestInstallRawBlobIsIdempotent` + `TestInstallRawBlobRefusals` prove the localstore delegation (double install agrees; forged claim, short/long/tampered bytes refuse); durability itself is the landed localstore discipline (purity bound for this package: no second write path). README package section added with test commands and no capability claim.\\n+- REV3 (rework of review RUN-260917-c05bc8): P1-a descriptor identity linked to the entry at build + evidence verification; P1-b AX number model + nested-duplicate refusal on extension values at build + decode; P2-f/P2-a environ gate adoption with the character string measure; P2-b/P2-c decode-side negatives for every surviving row + verifier/install negatives with per-plant logs; P2-d duplicate raw keys refused; P2-e identity re-decode before hashing; P3-b content XOR enforced; P3-c one-per-plan-candidate refused at build; P3-a sanitizer hardened with the exact bound stated; P3-d/P3-e harness rows fixed; P3-f/g/h hygiene. Finding-by-finding table in `TASK-260830-24z2b3_results.md`.\\n+- REV4 (rework of review RUN-260917-62d051; base refreshed 888ae3d→2fc6d50, authority now SPEC.v0.7.0 with byte-identical pinned sections): P1-c payload value model enforced for every event kind at build + decode with exact-int64 sealing (sealed bytes never round/collapse); P2-α one extension value-fault row per admission site (17 rows + 17 narrowing plants); P2-β decode duplicate-entry row; P2-γ duplicate plan keys refused; P3 null-content XOR, refusal-detail fixes, input_blocked/-(2^53)/U+2029/payload-top-dup/external-null-parent rows, EncodeNativeIdentity validation, N-main-count split, dead code removed, census version/not-array/maxima/overflow rows with the remainder stated as defense-in-depth. Finding-by-finding table in `TASK-260830-24z2b3_results.md`.\\n+- REV5 (rework of review RUN-260917-ab25c8; no base move, still 2fc6d50; every rev3 finding verified fixed, scope one P2 + four P3): P2-δ shared valid-UTF-8 text gate at every Build string admission (title, actor name/model, native_type, reason codes, exclusion_reason, generation, extension keys/values at any depth) plus `EncodeNativeIdentity` sanitizing both native keys before marshaling — invalid UTF-8 and lone surrogates refuse instead of sealing as U+FFFD, and the \\\"native\\\\xff\\\" vs \\\"native\\\\xfe\\\" collision pair both refuse; `TestBuildTextMustBeValidUTF8` (22 rows + collision pair) asserts the sealed bytes carry no U+FFFD, killed by the N-text-utf8 narrowing plant. P3: evidence archive rebuilt from a task-scoped dir (no foreign artifacts, no `__pycache__`); `-0`-only TRACEABILITY sentence first-hand verified (`+1`/`01` refuse \\\"not a JSON object\\\", `-0` passes the gate); build reason-duplicate row + N-reason-codes-dup-build plant; producer checklist rows only. Finding-by-finding table in `TASK-260830-24z2b3_results.md`.\\n+- BOUNDS (sibling scope, not waived): per-kind event payload fact registries past the envelope (which facts a kind may carry; the §1.6 value model on every payload member is enforced here); `maximal_safe` planning past the refusal gate; G2 admission past `RefuseUnstableForTarget`; Section 7.8 operation wiring (stays `sessadapter`). Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n+- AC: 18 of 18 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in `TASK-260830-24z2b3_conformance-matrix.md`).\\n+\\n ### TASK-260917-10k118: reconstructed the reviewed v0.7.0 adoption on trunk 7efe385 (STORY-260916-3uqbwq unlandable, accepted CRs frozen)\\n - METHOD: true pin delta is `git diff e4e3e88 9cb5dd4` (10 files) — the exported 238-file patch diffs unrelated tips and would revert five landed stories, so it was used as transport only; rev3 candidate bytes applied (15 modified + 3 new) with the 5 trunk-merged files copied verbatim after diff-review (no trunk test lost, `task-board.config.json` untouched). All 19 machine-applied files `cmp`-identical to the rev3 bytes; ownership sha256 `2548870d…8a5070`, projection digest `c4cd46bf…53473f6` recomputed two independent ways.\\n - RE-VERIFIED (this session, fresh clone + production helpers): tag `d4abe46f…795b3` Good, peeled `32b3f2ba…321834`, SPEC blob `c4903e60…1ddd86` 1185291 bytes sha256 `c6b2fe64…89ddcf` byte-identical to `SPEC.v0.7.0.md`; lock 64/64 rows order- and set-identical to the §1.5 table (1 known order normalization); 65/65 bindings + 132/132 cases carried with 3 reviewed additions each; all 49 discharged clauses re-measured (uniform +20/+79/+185/+281/+392, excerpts verbatim); rev3 prose says \\\"48 carried clause lines\\\" in two places — measured 49, matching the 49/569 numerator; artifact is right, prose miscounted.\\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\\nindex 55a228b..3309f7b 100644\\n--- a/README.md\\n+++ b/README.md\\n@@ -2394,6 +2394,33 @@ go test ./internal/matjournal -count=1 -cover\\n python3 internal/matjournal/mutant_harness.py\\n ```\\n \\n+## Clone Bundle and Canonical Session Types\\n+\\n+[`internal/clonebundle`](internal/clonebundle) validates and constructs\\n+the Section 13.14.1 clone capture contracts: Clone Raw Object Manifest\\n+1.0.0, Clone Capture Manifest 1.0.0 with its Capture Items, Capture\\n+Source Basis, and Capture Boundary, Canonical Session 1.0.0 with its\\n+Actors, Canonical Event 1.0.0 with Source Evidence and raw byte-range\\n+references, the NativeIdentity and WorkspaceBinding identities, and\\n+immutable source generations. Every Build entry produces byte-identical\\n+canonical bytes for identical inputs; every Decode entry enforces the\\n+closed shape, the class vocabularies, the included/excluded content\\n+rule, the core-derived `raw_complete` reconciliation, the stable-proof\\n+coupling, and the row-21 hosttrust exclusion allowlist. Blob Descriptor\\n+identity and byte-count agreement verify through `canonicaljson`, and\\n+blob bytes install only through the `localstore` no-replace discipline;\\n+the package performs no durable write itself. The clause map in\\n+[`internal/clonebundle/TRACEABILITY.md`](internal/clonebundle/TRACEABILITY.md)\\n+maps every pinned clause to its production entry and test, with the\\n+sibling-owned bounds stated. It adds no `ax` command, no `doctor`\\n+result, and no runtime capability claim.\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+go test ./internal/clonebundle -count=1\\n+go test ./internal/clonebundle -count=1 -cover\\n+PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/clonebundle/testdata/mutant_harness.py\\n+```\\n+\\n ## Crash/Restart Outcome Gate\\n \\n [`internal/crashgate`](internal/crashgate) executes the Section 13.13\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 10402,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2601,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
