nebundle; nothing imports clonebundle). The\n241|rev4 Change Request validation ran the 27-command suite with the landed\n242|`-timeout 25m` and is green (`ok internal/sessquery 390.722s` in the producer's\n243|cmd05). My own measurement on the pristine candidate copy\n244|(`logs/sessquery-race.log`): `go test ./internal/sessquery -race -count=1\n245|-timeout 25m` → `ok … 417.433s`, wall 419.6 s, exit 0, zero `DATA RACE` lines,\n246|host load 10.95 → 17.28 with another session's full `go test ./...` running\n247|concurrently (eight `.test` binaries alive mid-run); an idle host was not\n248|available. Three measurements under different load (rev2 390.6 s, rev3 347.4 s,\n249|rev4 417.4 s) all sit under the old 600 s default; the producer's earlier 665 s\n250|was under the full concurrent suite. Disposition unchanged: host-capacity\n251|artifact, not a candidate defect; the 25 m timeout on trunk (`888ae3d`) is the\n252|orchestration fix and the gate is green in this revision.\n253|\n254|## Rework scope (for the producer)\n255|\n256|1. P2-δ: a shared valid-UTF-8 text gate at every Build-side string admission;\n257|   sanitize `NativeSessionID` and `OpaqueIdentity` before `EncodeNativeIdentity`\n258|   marshals them (or validate them inside the exported entry); negatives at\n259|   `BuildCaptureManifest` (source identity native/opaque), `IdentityDigest`\n260|   (opaque) and one per Build shape, asserting no U+FFFD in the sealed bytes;\n261|   one narrowing mutant + harness row.\n262|2. P3-a″: rebuild the producer evidence archive from a task-scoped directory\n263|   (no foreign artifacts, no `__pycache__`).\n264|3. P3-b″: fix the `-0`/`+`/leading-zero sentence in TRACEABILITY.md.\n265|4. P3-c″: build-side reason-code duplicate row + harness row.\n266|5. P3-d″: re-complete only the producer checklist rows.\n267|\n268|Checklist state left by this review: the four reviewer rows (Implementation\n269|matches AC; Solution fits project architecture; Tests green; Gate … attacked