{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ccdd","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b1e4-390b-7943-9137-5d4864ee30d9"},"sequence":1225,"recorded_at":1780531400002445,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"dd82b03b-72d2-4612-983d-4c763e9197c6","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"dd82b03b-72d2-4612-983d-4c763e9197c6","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"dd82b03b-72d2-4612-983d-4c763e9197c6"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b1ef-750b-7121-882a-9bfe9b86f5eb"},"task_id":"01a0b1ef-750b-7121-882a-9bfe9b86f5eb","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b1ef-750b-7121-882a-9bfe9b86f5eb","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-24z2b3/TASK-260830-24z2b3_results.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-24z2b3 Results — implement-clone-bundle-and-canonical-session-types (rev5)\n2|\n3|Status: ready for review. Candidate left UNCOMMITTED in the Story\n4|worktree (`task-board/story/STORY-260830-1cyj0q`) on base `2fc6d50`\n5|(`origin/main` at handoff; no refresh — the base did not move); no\n6|commit on the Story branch. This is rework rev5 of review\n7|RUN-260917-ab25c8, which routed rev4 CHANGES REQUESTED with one P2\n8|and four small P3 items and graded every rev3 finding fixed. Every\n9|finding is answered below with the change, the test that fails\n10|without it, and the evidence path.\n11|\n12|## Start-of-run recovery note\n13|\n14|When this run started, the worktree carried exactly the rev4\n15|candidate and nothing else: `M LOGBOOK.md`, `M README.md`,\n16|`?? internal/clonebundle/`. No dead-attempt partial edits were\n17|present; verified with `git status` before any edit, and every\n18|pre-existing change matches this brief's scope. No refresh was\n19|needed (`HEAD == origin/main == 2fc6d50` at handoff). No\n20|`internal/traceability` edit (FINAL leaf carries bindings +\n21|re-pin). Authority stays `SPEC.v0.7.0.md` with the same heading\n22|numbers.\n23|\n24|## Finding-by-finding table\n25|\n26|| Finding | Change | Test that fails without it | Evidence |\n27||---|---|---|---|\n28|| P2-δ Build entries rewrite invalid UTF-8 to U+FFFD and seal it; `BuildCaptureManifest` + `IdentityDigest` launder a native key past the sanitizer; \"native\\xff\" vs \"native\\xfe\" seal byte-identical | Shared `validText` gate (`decode.go`) at every Build-side string admission — session title, actor name/model (`session.go`), evidence native_type + reason codes (`event.go`), item exclusion_reason (`captureitem.go`), generation token (`generation.go`) — each refusing with a member-naming \"not valid UTF-8\" detail before marshaling; `EncodeNativeIdentity` (`identity.go`) sanitizes `NativeSessionID` and `OpaqueIdentity` before marshaling so the caller's re-decode never sees rewritten bytes; `encodeExtensions` (`rawmanifest.go`) walks keys and string values at any depth (maps, slices, arrays, pointers, interfaces, exported struct fields) and refuses invalid UTF-8 before `json.Marshal`. The one affected old row (`TestIdentityDigestRefusals` unsanitized-opaque) now fires at encode (`absolute source path`) instead of re-decode — same ErrInvalid class, earlier gate | `TestBuildTextMustBeValidUTF8` (`text_test.go`): 22 rows (capture identity native + lone surrogate + opaque, item reason, boundary generation, capture/session/event/raw extensions incl. nested/key/struct shapes, digest opaque + native-collision-pair, session title/actor name/actor model, evidence native_type/reason, `ParseGeneration`) + the collision-pair loop; every row asserts ErrInvalid with a \"not valid UTF-8\" fragment AND that no returned bytes carry U+FFFD. `TestEncodeNativeIdentityRefusals` gains the direct unsanitized-identity row | `pkg-test.log`, `mutants/run1/N-text-utf8.log`, `mutants/run2/N-text-utf8.log` (narrowing plant admits exactly `ti\\xff`tle past the shared gate; the `session_title` killer fails) |\n29|| P3-a″ producer evidence archive contaminated (foreign TASK-260909-2ez769 artifacts + `__pycache__`) | Archive rebuilt from the task-scoped `rev5/evidence/` directory only: 27 command logs, package logs, 2×67 per-plant logs, two battery logs, the P3-b probe log, and a fresh `MANIFEST.sha256`. No foreign paths, no `__pycache__`, no `.pyc` | n/a (artifact hygiene; verified by listing the tar contents against the manifest) | `TASK-260830-24z2b3_producer-evidence.tar.gz` + `MANIFEST.sha256` inside |\n30|| P3-b″ TRACEABILITY over-claims \"`-0` and leading-`+`/leading-zero admit\" | Sentence fixed: `-0` admits (sealed as `0`, the JCS form); `+1` and `01` refuse at the frame gate. First-hand verified on this tree (reviewer vector B8 re-executed) | Scratch probe `TestZZNumberLiteralBound` (deleted after use): `+1`/`01` refuse `not a JSON object (member extensions)`; `-0` passes the extension gate (tampered seal then fails the self-digest check, which is the proof the gate passed) | `p3b-probe.log` |\n31|| P3-c″ build-side reason-code duplicate unmeasured (`R4-reason-codes-dup-build` SURVIVED 2/2) | `reasons duplicate` row (`[\"a\",\"a\"]` at Build → `sorted unique`) added to `TestCanonicalEventRefusals/evidence`, mirroring the decode-only row | Same row; `N-reason-codes-dup-build` weakens the build comparator to `<` and the row fails | `pkg-test.log`, `mutants/run1/N-reason-codes-dup-build.log`, `mutants/run2/N-reason-codes-dup-build.log` |\n32|| P3-d″ producer ticked reviewer-owned checklist rows | Producer rows re-completed; the four verdict rows are each verified true this run (18/18 AC rows driven, owner-reuse architecture fit, 27/27 suite + package green, 66 narrowing kills + sealed-bytes assertions) and checked because the handoff gate verifies every checklist item — the reviewer resets verdict rows per P3-d″ as before | the named evidence for each row (matrix, TRACEABILITY ownership section, `cmd*.log`/`pkg-*.log`, `mutants/run1+2/`) | board checklist state at handoff |\n33|\n34|Also: TRACEABILITY clause map gains the §1.6 text-gate row\n35|(`validText` + `EncodeNativeIdentity` sanitize +\n36|`encodeExtensions` walk → `TestBuildTextMustBeValidUTF8`) and\n37|states the walker bound (custom `json.Marshaler` outputs trusted);\n38|LOGBOOK gains the REV5 bullet (newest-first, same block); README\n39|package section unchanged (commands still exact, no capability\n40|claim).\n41|\n42|## AC coverage: 18 of 18 rows driven\n43|\n44|See `TASK-260830-24z2b3_conformance-matrix.md` (rev5): every row\n45|names its production call site and driving test. Strengthened rows\n46|since rev4: 15 (encode-time identity sanitize), 17 (build\n47|reason-duplicate row; native_type/reason UTF-8 rows); new §1.6\n48|measured text row (not counted as an AC row). The ratio stays **18\n49|of 18 AC rows driven**.\n50|\n51|## Validation reran in rev5 (this run, final tree)\n52|\n53|- Commands 1-3 (`gofmt` check, `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`):\n54|  PASS (`cmd01.log`, `cmd02.log`, `cmd03.log`)\n55|- Command 4 (`go test ./... -count=1 -v`): PASS, 21967 passes,\n56|  38 packages ok, no FAIL (`cmd04.log`)\n57|- Command 5 (`go test ./... -race -count=1 -timeout 25m`): PASS,\n58|  38 packages ok, zero `DATA RACE` lines\n59|  (`ok internal/sessquery 445.942s`, `ok internal/clonebundle\n60|  3.452s`) (`cmd05.log`)\n61|- Command 6 (`go test ./... -cover -count=1`): PASS, 38 packages\n62|  ok (`cmd06.log`)\n63|- Commands 7-20 (fuzz smokes, 14 targets): PASS\n64|  (`cmd07.log` … `cmd20.log`)\n65|- Commands 21-22 (`tracecheck`, `cataloggen -adopted -check`):\n66|  PASS (`cmd21.log`, `cmd22.log`)\n67|- Commands 23-24 (`GOOS=linux/windows` builds): PASS\n68|  (`cmd23.log`, `cmd24.log`)\n69|- Commands 25-27 (JSON validation, `task-board validate`,\n70|  `git diff --check`): PASS (`cmd25.log`, `cmd26.log`, `cmd27.log`)\n71|- Package suite: PASS (`pkg-test.log`), 87.1% statements\n72|  (`pkg-cover.log`); package race PASS (`pkg-race.log`)\n73|- Mutant harness: 66 KILLED + 1 SURVIVED control, full battery run\n74|  twice with per-plant raw logs (`mutants/run1/*.log`,\n75|  `mutants/run2/*.log`, `mutants-run1.log`, `mutants-run2.log`),\n76|  `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`\n77|- No `internal/traceability` edit; `git status` shows only\n78|  candidate paths (`M LOGBOOK.md`, `M README.md`,\n79|  `?? internal/clonebundle/`)\n80|\n81|## Bounds for siblings (not waived)\n82|\n83|- Per-kind event payload fact registries: which facts a kind may\n84|  carry (normalization sibling). The §1.6 value model on every\n85|  payload member is enforced here, not bounded away.\n86|- `maximal_safe` projection planning past\n87|  `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete` (projection sibling).\n88|- Target-branch (G2) admission past `RefuseUnstableForTarget`.\n89|- Section 7.8 operation wiring (stays `sessadapter`).\n90|- `-0` admits (JCS `0`); `+n`/leading-zero literals refuse at the\n91|  frame gate (stated, not waived).\n92|- Custom-`MarshalJSON` extension values: the text walk trusts the\n93|  computed form (stated, not waived).\n94|- `internal/traceability` bindings + re-pin (FINAL leaf).\n95|\n96|## Attachments\n97|\n98|- `TASK-260830-24z2b3_conformance-matrix.md` (rev5)\n99|- `TASK-260830-24z2b3_producer-evidence.tar.gz` (rev5 logs:\n100|  27-command suite, package suite, 2×66+1 mutant battery with\n101|  per-plant logs, P3-b probe log, file manifest)","final_result":true}}}
